From: NGM <ngm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ngm-compat: build ext/openssl against OpenSSL 3 (SSLv23 padding, SSLv3)

What: two things OpenSSL 3 (as we build it) no longer has.
 - ext/openssl/openssl.c: guard the OPENSSL_SSLV23_PADDING constant with
   #ifdef RSA_SSLV23_PADDING (removed in 3.0). Byte-identical to the hunk
   CloudLinux ships for 5.6/7.x as php-<ver>-fix-for-openssl-3.0.x.patch.
 - ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c: guard the SSLv3 client/server methods with
   #ifdef OPENSSL_NO_SSL3, raising the same "not compiled into the OpenSSL
   library" warning the SSLv2 branch already raises. Same shape as upstream
   PHP 5.6's xp_ssl.c. Without it the build links against
   SSLv3_{client,server}_method, which our OpenSSL lacks (GCC 14 reports the
   implicit declaration; ld fails). The method pointer becomes const, as
   OpenSSL has returned for years.

Why ours: CloudLinux builds ea-php53 only on EL8 (OpenSSL 1.1, which still
had both), so the 5.3 series has no OpenSSL-3 follow-up to its
php-5.3.29-openssl11.patch (force-kept). The former chrismfz/php53 fork
carried the same two guards in its tree.

Behaviour change: on OpenSSL 3, OPENSSL_SSLV23_PADDING is undefined and an
explicit sslv3:// stream fails with a warning instead of negotiating SSLv3.
Same as 5.6/7.x here.

Delete when: CloudLinux ships an OpenSSL-3 follow-up for ea-php53, or 5.3
is retired.
---
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
@@ -1180,7 +1180,9 @@
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("PKCS7_NOSIGS", PKCS7_NOSIGS, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_PKCS1_PADDING", RSA_PKCS1_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
+#ifdef RSA_SSLV23_PADDING
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_SSLV23_PADDING", RSA_SSLV23_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
+#endif
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_NO_PADDING", RSA_NO_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_PKCS1_OAEP_PADDING", RSA_PKCS1_OAEP_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 
--- a/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/xp_ssl.c
@@ -309,7 +309,7 @@
 		php_stream_xport_crypto_param *cparam
 		TSRMLS_DC)
 {
-	SSL_METHOD *method;
+	const SSL_METHOD *method;
 	
 	if (sslsock->ssl_handle) {
 		if (sslsock->s.is_blocked) {
@@ -338,9 +338,14 @@
 			break;
 #endif
 		case STREAM_CRYPTO_METHOD_SSLv3_CLIENT:
+#ifdef OPENSSL_NO_SSL3
+			php_error_docref(NULL TSRMLS_CC, E_WARNING, "SSLv3 support is not compiled into the OpenSSL library PHP is linked against");
+			return -1;
+#else
 			sslsock->is_client = 1;
 			method = SSLv3_client_method();
 			break;
+#endif
 		case STREAM_CRYPTO_METHOD_TLS_CLIENT:
 			sslsock->is_client = 1;
 			method = TLSv1_client_method();
@@ -350,9 +355,14 @@
 			method = SSLv23_server_method();
 			break;
 		case STREAM_CRYPTO_METHOD_SSLv3_SERVER:
+#ifdef OPENSSL_NO_SSL3
+			php_error_docref(NULL TSRMLS_CC, E_WARNING, "SSLv3 support is not compiled into the OpenSSL library PHP is linked against");
+			return -1;
+#else
 			sslsock->is_client = 0;
 			method = SSLv3_server_method();
 			break;
+#endif
 		case STREAM_CRYPTO_METHOD_SSLv2_SERVER:
 #if defined(OPENSSL_NO_SSL2) || OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x10100000L
 			php_error_docref(NULL TSRMLS_CC, E_WARNING, "SSLv2 support is not compiled into the OpenSSL library PHP is linked against");
